<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="b013102b">&lt;p&gt;
    Scorecards are platforms to communicate progress to technology and business and enable key stakeholders to make
    informed decisions. Scorecards leverage key performance indicators (“KPIs”) and general summaries of data to assist in
    the management of performance. Additionally, a scorecard typically links back to plans so that the performance can be
    measured against intended targets.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Typically, a benefits scorecard displays graphic indicators that visually convey the overall success or failure in
    achieving intended benefits of a program or project. They are based on a collection of key performance indicators
    (KPIs) used to assess the realization of previously identified program or project benefits.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p/&gt;&lt;p&gt;
    Typically, the benefits dashboards and scorecard display graphic indicators that visually convey the overall success or
    failure in achieving intended benefits of a program or project. They are based on a collection of key performance
    indicators (KPIs) used to assess the realization of previously identified program or project benefits.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="e593b8d9"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="cecc06b9"></attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="b395a2c6"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="e993e642">The purpose of a scorecard is to display progress over time.</attribute>
<attribute name="impactOfNotHaving" nodeId="b2edc87e"></attribute>
<attribute name="reasonsForNotNeeding" nodeId="65ab0cb7"></attribute>
<attribute name="briefOutline" nodeId="4a6f078f"></attribute>
<attribute name="representationOptions" nodeId="8aafe3a2">&lt;p&gt;
    Scorecards may either be communicated via PowerPoint, Excel or by using other methods such as a BI or a visualization
    tool.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    There are numerous vendor tools that can aid in the creation and maintenance of scorecards. These vendor tools allow
    for key features such as:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Data interactivity, analysis and visualization capabilities
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Importing, merging and analyzing data from the desktop, business intelligence or databases
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Optimizing outcomes through what-if analysis
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Establishing specific goals, defining how to measure success and communicating that information down through the
        organization
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Calculating performance and generating alerts when KPIs deviate from benchmarked values
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p/&gt;This work product&amp;nbsp;may often be combined with the benefits tracker.</attribute>
<attribute name="representation" nodeId="57787819"></attribute>
